# The files `make audit` reviews: one repo-relative path per line. `#` lines and blank lines are
# ignored. The runner refuses to start without this file, or with one that names a missing file.
#
# In scope: everything that reads from outside the process, decides what is shown, or decides what
# is built. That is all of the code, the manifest and the dependency policy.
#
# An excluded file is a line starting with `!`, then the path, then the reason. `make audit-checks`
# fails if a tracked .rs file is neither listed nor excluded, so a new file cannot go unreviewed
# by being forgotten.
#
# Not listed, each with its reason:
#   Cargo.lock        322 packages; cargo-deny reads it against RustSec, a model reading it adds nothing
#   scripts/, mk/     development tooling, never part of the binary, except the one script below that handles a key
#   docs/             recordings

